body:
Lists in markdown posts were rendering without bullets or numbering due to missing CSS specificity with Tailwind v4. Post layout had content left-aligned instead of centered with TOC sidebar.

## Changes

**Layout centering** (`app/posts/[...slug]/page.tsx`)
- Changed article container from `flex-1 min-w-0` to `w-full lg:max-w-3xl` 
- Added `lg:justify-center` to flex container
- TOC remains at fixed `w-80` on right

**List styling** (`app/globals.css`)
- Added explicit CSS rules for `.prose ul/ol` elements
- Set `list-style-type: disc` for unordered and `decimal` for ordered lists
- Added `padding-left: 1.5rem` and proper margins for indentation

```css
.prose ul {
  list-style-type: disc;
  padding-left: 1.5rem;
  margin-top: 1rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.prose ol {
  list-style-type: decimal;
  padding-left: 1.5rem;
  margin-top: 1rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
```

## Screenshots

**Before:** Lists rendering as plain text without bullets
![Before](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4349ae65-ba6d-44e8-9219-9863a3de1ed1)

**After:** Content centered with TOC on right, lists properly styled
